{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/navbar_readingbar

    The context bar (C2): the layer the navbar swaps to once the reader has scrolled past the page header,
    at the same 60px. The theme's core renderer appends it to navbar_plugin_output(), which Boost Union's
    navbar prints inside #usernavigation; scss/readingbar.scss positions it over the whole nav (nothing
    between the two is positioned) and hides it until amd/src/readingbar.js puts dimensions-ctx-on on the
    nav. Every decision is theme_dimensions\local\readingbar's.

    The left control opens the course index drawer with core's own toggler attributes, so Boost's
    drawers module does the work and remembers it as the last used toggle; it is drawn only where the
    drawer exists. The status is read-only: on 5.3 core's linear navigation footer owns the manual
    completion button, and the module follows its toggle event. Both labels are in the markup and the
    stylesheet shows the one data-state names, so the client composes no text. It is not core's
    data-region="completion-status": core's header module replaces the FIRST such element of the page,
    which would be this one.

    On a page that can switch into focus mode the layer carries the way in, the navbar's own entry form drawn a second
    time as an icon pill: amd/src/focusmode.js intercepts the submit of any form whose button carries its action, so
    the layer's switches in place exactly as the navbar's does, and without JavaScript both post to focus.php.

    A reader core lets edit the page gets core's edit mode switch at the end of the layer (D5): the layer
    covers the navbar's own switch while it is shown. It is core's edit_switch() output rendered a second
    time, with an id of its own, so its form, its React mount and core/edit_switch work as the first one
    does; the navbar's switch comes first in the document, so a lookup by the "Edit mode" label finds that one.

    Context variables required for this template (described without braces, because a Mustache
    comment closes at the first pair of closing braces it meets):

    * kind - activity or course
    * isactivity - Whether the page is an activity's
    * title - The activity's name, or the course's on the course page, plain
    * hassub - Whether the sub line has anything to say
    * coursename - The course's name on an activity page, plain; empty on the course page
    * progress - The reader's completion of the course ("X of Y completed"), plain; empty when not tracked
    * completed - The completed count the progress says, which the module moves on a completion toggle
    * total - The total count the progress says
    * hasindex - Whether the course index drawer exists on the page
    * drawerid - The course index drawer's id
    * hasstatus - Whether the reader's completion status of the activity is shown
    * cmid - The activity's course module id
    * state - complete or pending
    * complete - Whether the state is complete
    * hasfocus - Whether the page can switch into focus mode
    * focus - The navbar's focus mode entry form: actionurl, sesskey, cmid, label, title
    * canedit - Whether the reader may edit the page, by core's own predicate
    * editswitch - Core's edit mode switch as core_renderer::edit_switch() renders it, trusted HTML

    Example context (json):
    {
        "kind": "activity",
        "isactivity": true,
        "title": "Reading 2: Competency maps",
        "hassub": true,
        "coursename": "Competency management",
        "progress": "4 of 9 completed",
        "completed": 4,
        "total": 9,
        "hasindex": true,
        "drawerid": "theme_boost-drawers-courseindex",
        "hasstatus": true,
        "cmid": 42,
        "state": "pending",
        "complete": false,
        "hasfocus": true,
        "focus": {
            "actionurl": "https://example.com/theme/dimensions/focus.php",
            "sesskey": "abc123",
            "cmid": 42,
            "label": "Focus mode",
            "title": "Read this activity without distractions"
        },
        "canedit": true,
        "editswitch": "<form action=\"https://example.com/editmode.php\" method=\"post\" class=\"d-flex align-items-center editmode-switch-form ms-2\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"switch\" name=\"setmode\" id=\"editingswitch1\"><label for=\"editingswitch1\">Edit mode</label></form>"
    }
}}
<div class="dimensions-ctxbar" data-region="dimensions-ctxbar" data-kind="{{kind}}">
    {{#hasindex}}
    <button type="button" class="btn dimensions-ctxbar-index" data-region="dimensions-ctxbar-index"
        data-toggler="drawers" data-action="toggle" data-target="{{drawerid}}"
        aria-label="{{#str}} opendrawerindex, core {{/str}}" title="{{#str}} opendrawerindex, core {{/str}}">
        <i class="icon fa fa-list-ul fa-fw" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </button>
    {{/hasindex}}
    <div class="dimensions-ctxbar-text">
        <span class="dimensions-ctxbar-title" data-region="dimensions-ctxbar-title">{{title}}</span>
        {{#hassub}}
        <span class="dimensions-ctxbar-sub" data-region="dimensions-ctxbar-sub">{{#coursename}}{{coursename}}{{#progress}} · {{/progress}}{{/coursename}}{{#progress}}<span data-region="dimensions-ctxbar-progress" data-completed="{{completed}}" data-total="{{total}}">{{progress}}</span>{{/progress}}</span>
        {{/hassub}}
    </div>
    {{#hasstatus}}
    <span class="dimensions-ctxbar-status" data-region="dimensions-ctxbar-status" data-cmid="{{cmid}}" data-state="{{state}}">
        <span class="dimensions-ctxbar-status-complete">
            <i class="icon fa fa-check fa-fw" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{#str}} readingbar_status_complete, theme_dimensions {{/str}}
        </span>
        <span class="dimensions-ctxbar-status-pending">{{#str}} readingbar_status_pending, theme_dimensions {{/str}}</span>
    </span>
    {{/hasstatus}}
    {{#hasfocus}}
    {{#focus}}
    <form class="dimensions-ctxbar-focus" data-region="dimensions-ctxbar-focus" method="post" action="{{actionurl}}">
        <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
        <input type="hidden" name="cmid" value="{{cmid}}">
        <input type="hidden" name="action" value="enter">
        <button type="submit" class="btn dimensions-ctxbar-focus-button" data-action="dimensions-focus-enter"
            aria-label="{{label}}" title="{{title}}">
            <i class="icon fa-solid fa-book-open-reader fa-fw" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        </button>
    </form>
    {{/focus}}
    {{/hasfocus}}
    {{#canedit}}
    <div class="dimensions-ctxbar-edit" data-region="dimensions-ctxbar-edit">{{{editswitch}}}</div>
    {{/canedit}}
</div>
